<% content_for :title, "Carousel CSV import and export" %>
<h1>Carousel CSV import and export</h1>
<p>Export all carousel fields, edit the spreadsheet, then upload or paste the CSV for review. Figures, seats, and placement history are not included.</p>
<p><%= link_to "Download carousel CSV", export_carousel_csv_path, class: "button" %></p>
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Before importing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Leave ID, slug, and updated_at unchanged for existing carousels; leave them blank for new rows. Omitted rows are never deleted.</li>
    <li>Blank cells and omitted columns leave existing values unchanged. Enter <code>__CLEAR__</code> to clear an optional value; enter <code>\__CLEAR__</code> for that literal text.</li>
    <li>Use the maker IDs below. Ring columns A through F describe independently sourced ring research. Sources are required for published counts and ring details.</li>
    <li>Known layout dimensions cannot be changed here. Adding both dimensions to an unknown layout creates unknown seats.</li>
    <li>Keep the csv_format column and any leading apostrophes in exported cells: these protect spreadsheet text and enable round trips. Use UTF-8 CSV and preserve text formatting.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Imports are limited to 1 MB, 5,000 rows, and 10,000 newly generated seats. Preview expires after 30 minutes. <%= link_to "Import instructions", "#{editor_guide_path}#carousel-csv" %></p>
</section>
<%= render "form", csv_text: params[:csv_text] %>
<% if Maker.exists? %>
  <details>
    <summary>Maker IDs</summary>
    <table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Maker</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><% Maker.order(:name, :id).each do |maker| %><tr><td><%= maker.id %></td><td><%= maker.name %></td></tr><% end %></tbody>
    </table>
  </details>
<% end %>
